                    {
                        "sense_id": "569b70ba-3cae-3dfe-a16d-ed3b3f267fd0",
                        "entry_id": "7b91ccda-6982-36c1-b5bd-9ee88603577b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To untwist, uncoil, or untwine (something wreathed)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ac75e70-10c4-4bcc-a86b-0ac86d28c5c7",
                                "sense_id": "569b70ba-3cae-3dfe-a16d-ed3b3f267fd0",
                                "text": "But sin it is, no less;—a blot, foul as the crater-pool of hell; it puts out the sun at noon; it parches all fertility; and, conscience or no conscience—ere he die—let every master who wrenches bond-babe from mother, that the nipple tear; unwreathes the arms of sisters; or cuts the holy unity in twain; till apart fall man and wife, like one bleeding body cleft"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "444b41c6-677c-4b65-914e-48f7a99f21f7",
                                "sense_id": "569b70ba-3cae-3dfe-a16d-ed3b3f267fd0",
                                "text": "Yes, our last farewell is breathed,\nAnd we part, for ever part;\nEvery tie is now unwreathed\nWhich had bound us heart to heart;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c50c2af-cfc0-4b1e-8289-c37061a601b5",
                                "sense_id": "569b70ba-3cae-3dfe-a16d-ed3b3f267fd0",
                                "text": "the splendid rhythms and harmonies that wreathed and unwreathed themselves in his mind"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
